  "summary_en": "Policy brief by Paradigm Initiative recommending that Nigeria's forthcoming national AI strategy be grounded in constitutional human rights, data protection, algorithmic accountability, and transparency. It urges comprehensive data legislation, an ombudsman, limits on AI in law enforcement, local AI procurement safeguards, and large-scale upskilling.",
  "title_clean": "Towards A Rights-Respecting Artificial Intelligence Policy for Nigeria",
  "title_en": "Towards A Rights-Respecting Artificial Intelligence Policy for Nigeria",
  "venue": "Paradigm Initiative",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "National AI policy should align with constitutional rights to privacy, non-discrimination and dignity.",
   "Nigeria needs comprehensive national data legislation and a data governance ombudsman.",
   "Limit or justify AI use in law enforcement, criminal justice, immigration and national security.",
   "Transparent procurement of foreign AI with algorithmic accountability and knowledge transfer.",
   "Expand digital upskilling and reskilling to address youth unemployment and job displacement."
